# markdown-syntax AST->HTML conformance suite v1
source: gfm_strikethrough
count: 6

--- case 1 options - label-bytes 38 input-bytes 7 expected-bytes 14
should ignore strikethrough by default
--- input
a ~b~ c
--- expected
<p>a ~b~ c</p>
--- end
--- case 2 options gfm label-bytes 42 input-bytes 7 expected-bytes 21
should support strikethrough w/ two tildes
--- input
a ~~b~~
--- expected
<p>a <del>b</del></p>
--- end
--- case 3 options gfm label-bytes 48 input-bytes 9 expected-bytes 16
should not support strikethrough w/ three tildes
--- input
a ~~~b~~~
--- expected
<p>a ~~~b~~~</p>
--- end
--- case 4 options gfm label-bytes 51 input-bytes 11 expected-bytes 24
should support strikethrough after an escaped tilde
--- input
a \~~~b~~ c
--- expected
<p>a ~<del>b</del> c</p>
--- end
--- case 5 options gfm label-bytes 35 input-bytes 17 expected-bytes 38
should support nested strikethrough
--- input
a ~~b ~~c~~ d~~ e
--- expected
<p>a <del>b <del>c</del> d</del> e</p>
--- end
--- case 6 options gfm,single_tilde_off label-bytes 69 input-bytes 13 expected-bytes 27
should not support strikethrough w/ one tilde if `singleTilde: false`
--- input
a ~b~ ~~c~~ d
--- expected
<p>a ~b~ <del>c</del> d</p>
--- end
